Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 02:23:36 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Hide host-owned controls when framed: ?embed=1
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

With ?lang= and ?theme= a host decides what the app starts with, but the app
still renders its own language menu and theme switch. The reader then has two
switches for one setting, and the one they reach for first is the one that loses
on the next load, because the host reapplies its choice. This adds ?embed=1 to
hide the two controls a host has taken over.

Deliberately narrow, and it is not a kiosk mode:

- Settings stays. It is the only route to provider configuration, and a host
  cannot offer that on the app's behalf. Hiding it would strand the user.
- Attribution stays. Nothing here removes the project's name from the page.

useIsEmbedded resolves after mount rather than during render: the server has no
query string, so branching inline would hydrate differently than it rendered.

The language gate lives inside LanguageSwitcher rather than at each call site,
because that pill is rendered from three places — the home page, the classroom
header and the Pro rail — and a host that supplied ?lang= wants it gone from all
of them. Theme has no such single component: the Pro rail uses ThemeToggle while
the home page and classroom header each build their own inline menu, so all
three are gated separately.

Verified on a dev server with ?lang=th&theme=dark&embed=1: the control pill goes
from three buttons to one (Settings), while the Thai locale and the dark class
both remain applied — the host's choices survive, only its duplicated controls
are gone.
